ed solution within NestJS            | Maximum flexibility for the required invite-only flow.     |\\n| **Content Management**| Strapi (Headless CMS, self-hosted)                 | User-friendly for non-technical editors, rapid setup.      |\\n| **CI/CD**             | AWS CodePipeline, AWS CDK (TypeScript for IaC)     | Full automation of testing and deployment.                 |\\n\\n### 3. Execution Phases\\n\\n**Phase 1: Foundational Setup (Infrastructure & Backend)**\\n1.  **Infrastructure:** Provision the core AWS environment using AWS CDK.\\n    - Create a new VPC with public and private subnets across multiple Availability Zones.\\n    - Deploy the Amazon Aurora Serverless v2 PostgreSQL database into private subnets.\\n    - Set up AWS Secrets Manager for storing database credentials.\\n    - Configure initial IAM roles and policies with least-privilege access.\\n2.  **Backend:** Develop the core application and authentication.\\n    - Initialize the NestJS project with all required dependencies.\\n    - Establish the Prisma schema for `User` and other core models.\\n    - Implement the secure, invite-only user registration flow.\\n    - Implement the JWT-based login/logout/refresh endpoints.\\n    - Create Role-Based Access Control (RBAC) guards (`resident`, `admin`).\\n\\n**Phase 2: Content & Frontend Shell (Content Management & Frontend)**\\n1.  **Content Management:** Deploy and configure the Strapi CMS.\\n    - Provision a small, cost-effective host for the Strapi Docker container.\\n    - Define the 'News & Events' content type within the Strapi admin panel.\\n    - Configure public API access for published content.\\n    - Set up a webhook to be triggered upon content changes.\\n2.  **Frontend:** Initialize the project and build the main user interface structure.\\n    - Initialize the React project using Vite.\\n    - Build the primary `AppShell` component (Header, Footer, Navigation).\\n    - Implement client-side routing using React Router, including `AuthGuard` components for protected routes.\\n    - Connect the frontend to the backend's authentication endpoints (Login, Logout). Implement global state management for user authentication status.\\n\\n**Phase 3: Feature Implementation & Integration (All Teams)**\\n1.  **Backend:** Build out all required API endpoints as defined in the plan (e.g., for documents, user profiles, etc.).\\n2.  **Frontend:** Build all individual pages.\\n    - **Public Pages:** 'Contact Us', 'Bylaws', 'Schools'. Fetch data from the backend API where necessary.\\n    - **Protected Pages:** 'Dues', 'Annual Meetings'. These pages will be wrapped by the `AuthGuard`.\\n    - **News & Events Page:** Fetch and display content from the Strapi API.\\n3.  **Integration:** Connect all frontend components to their corresponding backend and Strapi API endpoints.\\n\\n**Phase 4: Deployment, Testing & Handoff**\\n1.  **Infrastructure:** Finalize and deploy the full CI/CD pipeline in AWS CodePipeline.\\n    - The pipeline will automatically test and deploy the backend to AWS Lambda and the frontend to S3/CloudFront.\\n    - Configure the production API Gateway to use a Lambda authorizer for validating JWTs from the backend.\\n2.  **Testing:** Conduct comprehensive end-to-end testing of all user flows, including registration, login, accessing protected content, and form submissions.\\n3.  **Handoff:** Create a simple user guide for the non-technical administrator on how to use the Strapi CMS to add and update 'News & Events' articles. Deliver the final, deployed website.\\n---END FILE CONTENT---\"}]}],\"config\":{},\"tools\":[],\"output\":{}}","genkit:output":"{\"candidates\":[{\"index\":0,\"finishReason\":\"stop\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"APPROVE\"}]},\"custom\":{}}],\"usage\":{\"inputTokens\":1422,\"outputTokens\":85,\"totalTokens\":1507},\"custom\":{\"id\":\"chatcmpl-BxHIPEnkkZ8LZZmnwJ9DSrrgkdd4i\",\"object\":\"chat.completion\",\"created\":1753467537,\"model\":\"o